  "title": "Investigating the Association Between Fast-Paced Environments and ADHD Development in Pupils",
  "objective": "To examine whether exposure to fast-paced environments during childhood is associated with an increased likelihood of developing attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder (ADHD).",
  "background": "Attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder (ADHD) is a neurodevelopmental disorder characterized by symptoms of inattention, hyperactivity, and impulsivity. While genetic and neurological factors are known to play a role, environmental influences have also been implicated in its development. Recent studies suggest that early-life exposure to high-stimulus or fast-paced environments may contribute to neurobiological changes that increase vulnerability to ADHD.",
  "research_questions": [
    "Is there a correlation between early-life exposure to fast-paced environments and the diagnosis of ADHD?",
